   "body": "In the spike's race test on MinIO, 8 Mojo writers to one table exhausted their commit retries 58 times in 160 writes. Nothing was lost, because the step's next attempt commits, but each one costs a whole step attempt. Look at the retry count and backoff (jitter) for object-store catalogs, and whether listing by key prefix (which the spike found reliable on MinIO) is what morca uses.\n\nFound in the iceberg-rust spike (#520, spikes/iceberg-rust/README.md, PR #529).",
