   "body": "## Summary\n\nThe Iceberg sink commits through a Hive Metastore with our own `HmsCommitCatalog` (`crates/common/iceberg/src/hms.rs`, about 900 lines, added in #977 and shipped in #986), because iceberg-rust's `HmsCatalog::update_table` still returns `FeatureUnsupported` (\"Updating a table is not supported yet\", iceberg-catalog-hms 0.10.1).\n\nThe code is a **stopgap**. HMS commits belong in iceberg-rust, and we should not carry our own commit protocol for another project's table format for longer than we have to.\n\n## Motivation\n\n- **Reliability and maintenance:** the code owns lock handling, the optimistic metadata-location check, retry classification and the \"metastore never answered\" case. Those are the places where a subtle bug corrupts a table, and upstream gives them wider review.\n- **Coupling:** it relies on iceberg-rust internals (`TableCommit::apply`, the HMS catalog's transport setup), so an iceberg-rust release can break it.\n- **Duplication:** once upstream supports HMS commits, we would have two implementations.\n\n## Proposed plan\n\n1. **Upstream it.** Open an issue and a PR on `apache/iceberg-rust` adding `update_table` to `iceberg-catalog-hms`. Base it on our implementation, which follows Iceberg Java's `HiveTableOperations`: an exclusive table lock, reload and apply the commit, write the next metadata file, check that `metadata_location` is still the base, `alter_table` with `DO_NOT_UPDATE_STATS`, then unlock.\n2. **On each iceberg-rust release,** check whether `HmsCatalog::update_table` is implemented.\n3. **When it is,** delete `HmsCommitCatalog` and build the plain `HmsCatalog` again in `faucet-common-iceberg`'s `build_hms`, keeping `hms.lock-timeout-ms` only if upstream offers an equivalent.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Locking:** if upstream commits without taking the metastore table lock, a mixed rollout (an old faucet using our lock, a new one using upstream's) would not coordinate. Check upstream's locking before switching, and document it in the release notes if it differs.\n- **Table properties:** upstream must write the same `metadata_location` / `previous_metadata_location` table parameters. Otherwise tables written before and after the switch read differently.\n- **Hive column list:** our commit also rewrites the Hive column list from the Iceberg schema, mapping zoned timestamps to `timestamp with local time zone`. Check that upstream does the same, or that dropping it changes nothing faucet relies on.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- An upstream iceberg-rust issue or PR exists and is linked here.\n- When an iceberg-rust release supports HMS commits, `HmsCommitCatalog` is removed and `crates/sink/iceberg/tests/integration_hms.rs` passes against the upstream catalog, including `concurrent_hms_writers_both_commit`.\n- `.claude/rules` / crate READMEs no longer describe our own HMS commit path.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nOther iceberg-rust gaps (schema widening, equality-delete upsert, overwrite, Hive 4); those are tracked in #982, #225 and #179.\n\n## References\n\n#977, #986, #982. Rule this follows: a missing library feature is noted and decided before it is built ourselves.\n",
